teemerchant is distributed under the MIT license in LICENSE.

Portable HTTP releases bundle CPython (PSF), PyInstaller (GPL with bootloader
exception), cryptography (Apache/BSD), httpx and their dependencies. Their bundled
license notices are in licenses/python and licenses/Python-LICENSE.txt.

TEE verification uses teemerchant's in-process native library, derived from the
MIT-licensed teeproxy verifier; attribution and pinned source provenance remain
in native/NOTICE. Native dependency notices accompany binary releases.

The private VLESS helper is derived from teerouter's MIT-licensed egress helper
and embeds the pinned Xray/Go dependencies recorded in egress/go.mod and go.sum.
Their upstream licenses accompany the release under licenses/egress.

No Electron, merchant credentials, platform secrets, TEE policy, or deployment
configuration is included in public binary releases.
